<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Earhart called the clinic and was seen the same day. She flew yesterday as a passenger on an airline flight to visit her sister, on the third day of a head cold. During the descent her left ear blocked and became very painful; swallowing and yawning did not clear it. The pain has eased to an ache, but the ear feels full and sounds are muffled, and her own voice sounds loud in that ear. She has had no spinning, unsteadiness, ringing, discharge from the ear, or fever. Her right ear cleared normally. The cold has added clear drainage and a scratchy throat to her usual blockage. She has kept up the saline rinses and fluticasone, has not used any decongestant, and has not flown as a pilot since the endoscopy. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>During the descent of an airline flight yesterday</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Left ear</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>About 20 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Sharp pain on descent, now a dull ache with fullness and muffled hearing</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Pain 3 of 10 now; 8 of 10 on descent</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Third day of a head cold; chronic rhinosinusitis on saline and fluticasone</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Swallowing and yawning did not clear it</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No vertigo, ringing, discharge, or fever</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

