    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 2026-07-20; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Well; temperature 37.1 °C, pulse 74, blood pressure 112/70</td></tr><tr><td>Ears</td><td>Left tympanic membrane retracted, with a small hemorrhage within the drum and an amber fluid line behind it; no perforation. Right tympanic membrane normal</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>512 Hz tuning fork: Weber lateralizes to the left; Rinne negative on the left and positive on the right, consistent with a conductive loss on the left</td></tr><tr><td>Nose and throat</td><td>Swollen turbinates with clear mucus; mild redness of the throat</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>No nystagmus; Romberg normal; facial movement normal</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

